One-time steps for the users' home settings (T051), run by
/usr/libexec/arkadeos/migrate at login, each once per user, in name order:
NNN-what-it-does.sh, sourced in bash with set_default and replace_app
available (see migrate). A new user gets the new defaults from /etc/xdg anyway,
so a step only has to bring an existing user from the old default to the new
one, and must leave alone what the user changed.

A step that scripts the desktop goes through /usr/libexec/arkadeos/plasma-script,
never straight to PlasmaShell.evaluateScript: Plasma answers before it has
loaded its taskbar, and a script run then changes nothing yet succeeds
(steps 008 and 010 on Roland's laptop, 2026-11-15).

early/: steps run before the desktop starts (migrate --early,
arkadeos-migrate-early.service), on the setting files themselves. A widget
or anything else the desktop loads leaves the image only together with an
early step that takes it out of the users' files, so the desktop never
loads it broken.
